/**
\fn pdg::Animated::addAnimationHelper(IAnimationHelper helper)
\brief Register a callback after the object's normal animation step.

The callback runs as `callback.call(helper, owner, deltaSeconds)` and returns a
boolean: true keeps its registration, false retires it. Helpers run in registration
order. Adding the same helper twice to one owner has no effect; a helper may also
be registered on several owners. A retained helper can be added again after it finishes.

Callbacks may remove themselves, remove another helper, or clear the owner's
helpers. Removed callbacks do not run later in the same step. Additions first run
on the next step. Removing and re-adding the current helper creates a new
registration, which is unaffected by the old callback returning false.

\param helper An IAnimationHelper constructed from a callback. Active registrations
retain it. After retirement, normal JavaScript references determine its lifetime.
\return The original owner object, for chaining.

\par Example
\code{.js}
const helper = new pdg.IAnimationHelper(function(owner, deltaSeconds) {
    owner.rotateBy(deltaSeconds * 0.5);
    return true;
});
sprite.addAnimationHelper(helper).setMovement(20, 0);
// Later: sprite.removeAnimationHelper(helper);
\endcode
\see removeAnimationHelper(), clearAnimationHelpers(), IAnimationHelper
*/
